#> 2020-08-15.4           0.4                0 2020-08-15      4
#> 2020-08-16.1           0.1               15 2020-08-16      1
#> 2020-08-16.2           0.2                6 2020-08-16      2
#> 2020-08-16.3           0.3                6 2020-08-16      3
#> 2020-08-16.4           0.4                6 2020-08-16      4
#> 2020-08-17.1           0.1               60 2020-08-17      1
#> 2020-08-17.2           0.2               26 2020-08-17      2
#> 2020-08-17.3           0.3                9 2020-08-17      3
#> 2020-08-17.4           0.4                3 2020-08-17      4



But I think there is something going on upstream. You have nested loops 
by/lapply and it is probably possible to avoid further processing.
It might be useful to run a couple of iterations of the lapply loop and 
post the output of that in dput format (before by()).

Hope this helps,

Rui Barradas


